 \nCategories: free\nSource: funcheap/san-jose\n\nOur Story: Father and son
  duo Mike and Abel Barrera\, started The Bernal Scream as a free show in t
 heir backyard in 2013. Over the next couple years The Bernal Scream would 
 see thousands of people\, countless terrifying scares\, TV news coverage\,
  and endless online articles. Riding the momentum of this ongoing build of
  success\, it was finally time to take The Bernal Scream out of their back
 yard and into the commercial spotlight. In 2016 the father-and-son duo had
  managed to cement its name as one of the Bay Area’s premier commercial 
 haunted attractions. Their breakout show “Satan’s Revenge” would rai
 se the bar and instill a new kind of fear in the scene. Thousands more wou
 ld turn out that year to experience this special show for themselves. Foll
 owing their success in 2016\, the duo would take some time off to spend ti
 me as a family. During that period\, however\, their lives would change fo
 rever when Father/Co-Founder Abel Barrera was diagnosed with stage four pa
 ncreatic cancer. The passing of their father (co-founder) Abel Barrera wou
 ld rock the family down to the core. Prior to Abel Barrera’s passing\, t
 he duo would spend their remaining time together building for what should 
 have been
LOCATION:san jose
