 h-bay+funcheap/san-francisco\n\nImprov Legends Shaun Landry & Hans Summers
  Return to the San Francisco Bay Area for Two Nights They will be at Oakla
 nd’s Pan Theater for two nights only: September 18 & 19 OAKLAND\, CA —
  August 21\, 2026 — Pan Theater will host improv legends Shaun Landry an
 d Hans Summers for two performances on Friday\, September 18\, and Saturda
 y\, September 19\, at 8:00 p.m. Landry will also lead her award-winning wo
 rkshop\, The Art of the Improvised Monologue\, on Saturday\, September 19\
 , from 1:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. The Second City alums have been performing t
 ogether since 1986. Landry and Summers founded Oui Be Negroes\, America’
 s first almost all Black improv troupe\, and trained during Chicago’s ea
 rly improv renaissance under Del Close and other pioneers of the art form.
  Both have taught and performed at iO\, iO West\, The Second City\, and ot
 her leading institutions\, and their work is documented in Amy E. Seham’
 s acclaimed improv history\, Whose Improv Is It Anyway?: Beyond Second Cit
 y. “Their work reminds us of what improvisational theater can be. It sho
 ws us the power improv has to make audiences think\, to transform people\,
 ” said Pan Theater founder David Alger. “For Bay Area performers and a
 udiences\, g
LOCATION:Pan Theater\, 120 Frank Ogawa Plaza\, Oakland\, CA Tickets: $20 (
 General Admission)
