 733 Stoneridge Drive\, Pleasant\nPrice: Free\nCategories: community\, free
 \nSource: funcheap/east-bay\n\nPacific Pearl Shopping Center invites famil
 ies and community members to welcome the season at its Mid-Autumn Moon Fes
 tival on Saturday\, September 19\, from 1 to 3 p.m. The free celebration w
 ill take place near 85 Degrees Cafe at the Pleasanton shopping center. Gue
 sts can enjoy an energetic lion dance presented by FlyU After School\, a m
 artial-arts presentation by Pallen’s Martial Arts Tri Valley\, face pain
 ting\, a balloon artist and a hands-on craft station for children. The aft
 ernoon is designed to bring neighbors together for a lively celebration in
 spired by the Mid-Autumn Festival’s traditions of family\, community and
  togetherness. “Pacific Pearl is proud to create welcoming experiences t
 hat reflect the cultures and traditions represented throughout the Tri-Val
 ley\,” said Brandi Hardy\, Director of Marketing for Pacific Pearl. “W
 e look forward to gathering with families for an afternoon filled with col
 or\, creativity and memorable performances.” Admission is free. Activiti
 es and craft materials will be available while supplies last. Guests are e
 ncouraged to arrive early and make an afternoon of the celebration by expl
 oring Pacific Pearl’s diverse collection of restaurants\, specialty f
LOCATION:Pacific Pearl\, near 85 Degrees Bakery Cafe\, 2693–2733 Stoneri
 dge Drive\, Pleasant
